<title>MEXICO: INTERVIEW-Vitro seeks to reduce debt in 97.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-Vitro seeks to reduce debt in 97.</headline>
<byline>Daniel Perez-Whitaker</byline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glass giant Vitro closed a stormy chapter in its history last week after finalizing the sale of its troubled U.S. subsidiary Anchor Glass Corp.</p>
<p>Vitro sold the glass company to Consumers Packaging and Owens-Brockway for $392 million, a sum used to repay Anchor's creditors. The Mexican company purchased Anchor Glass in August 1989 in a hostile takeover for about $950 million in equity and debt.</p>
</text>
